# ===========================================================================
# IntoTheDarkness — leak-site monitoring. SOURCE OF TRUTH for this schedule.
# Append to the user crontab (do NOT replace it; other projects live there):
#     (crontab -l; cat deploy/crontab) | crontab -
# Then verify:  crontab -l
#
# Sweeps run at 06:00, 10:00 and 14:00 US Eastern. The 06:00 sweep always
# mails the full report, even with nothing new (ITD_DIGEST_HOURS); the others
# mail only when there is something to say.
#
# The hour is decided inside monitor-run.sh, not here, so cron fires hourly
# and --scheduled returns immediately on the other 21 hours. Ubuntu's cron
# (3.0pl1) has no CRON_TZ, and `Linger=no` on this box rules out a systemd
# timer with its own timezone, so this is the one arrangement that follows
# EDT/EST on its own and keeps 6am at 6am all year. Change the hours with
# ITD_RUN_HOURS in the script, not by editing this line.
#
# Cron fires every 15 minutes: the scheduled sweeps run at :00 of their hours,
# and in between the script runs a watchlist-only sweep every
# ITD_WATCHLIST_INTERVAL_MINUTES (from .env, default 60) that alerts only on
# priority vendors. Silence means it ran and found nothing. Tor trouble, a failed sweep or a
# self-healed Tor all send mail — see deploy/ops_notify.py.
# ===========================================================================
*/15 * * * * /home/user/.claude/projects/ai-intothedarkness/deploy/monitor-run.sh --scheduled
